We're excited about that.

22
00:00:43,540 --> 00:00:45,760
But this morning, we're wrapping up our parable series.

23
00:00:45,760 --> 00:00:47,580
And remember, just as a recap,

24
00:00:47,580 --> 00:00:49,860
the parables are aimed at stopping us in our tracks.

25
00:00:49,860 --> 00:00:55,000
Their intent is to make us feel uneasy at first

26
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,440
as we wrestle with the story that Jesus is giving us,

27
00:00:58,440 --> 00:01:02,960
the kingdom reality below that lesson.

28
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:05,920
And we've said that the parables

29
00:01:05,920 --> 00:01:07,740
really have three main themes in them,

30
00:01:07,740 --> 00:01:09,680
at least for our purposes in this series.

31
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:12,620
They introduce the surprising arrival of the kingdom,

32
00:01:12,620 --> 00:01:15,540
that the kingdom of God is coming in unexpected ways,

33
00:01:15,540 --> 00:01:19,080
in ways that the nation of Israel wasn't expecting,

34
00:01:19,080 --> 00:01:21,040
in small, surprising ways,

35
00:01:21,680 --> 00:01:23,560
like a seed planted in a field,

36
00:01:23,560 --> 00:01:25,160
like lemon spreads through dough.

37
00:01:25,160 --> 00:01:27,840
It's small and insignificant on the surface,

38
00:01:27,840 --> 00:01:29,440
but it is unstoppable

39
00:01:29,440 --> 00:01:31,800
as it gets a hold of the hearts

40
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:33,620
of those who have embraced God's kingdom.

41
00:01:33,620 --> 00:01:36,360
It is a surprising arrival with a surprising ethic.

42
00:01:36,360 --> 00:01:41,100
It demands sacrificial love and obedience.

43
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:43,940
It lays down our lives for those around us.

44
00:01:43,940 --> 00:01:47,280
And because it's surprising in its arrival

45
00:01:47,280 --> 00:01:48,920
and it's surprising in its ethic,

46
00:01:48,920 --> 00:01:51,340
it presents us with a crisis of choice.

47
00:01:51,340 --> 00:01:54,940
What will we do with the story of the kingdom of God?

48
00:01:54,940 --> 00:01:56,080
Will we embrace it?

49
00:01:56,080 --> 00:01:59,020
And will we live into it with our whole lives?

50
00:01:59,020 --> 00:02:01,560
Or will we reject it?

51
00:02:01,560 --> 00:02:03,580
Because those really are the only two choices.

52
00:02:03,580 --> 00:02:05,360
I know in American Christianity,

53
00:02:05,360 --> 00:02:07,380
we like to provide a third choice

54
00:02:07,380 --> 00:02:10,260
where we can kind of be in and kind of be out,

55
00:02:10,260 --> 00:02:11,520
one foot in, one foot out,

56
00:02:11,520 --> 00:02:14,640
sitting on the fence, celebrating Jesus,

57
00:02:14,840 --> 00:02:15,780
being a fan of Jesus,

58
00:02:15,780 --> 00:02:18,280
but not really taking seriously, obeying Jesus.

59
00:02:18,280 --> 00:02:21,940
And the parables just don't really give us that option, right?

60
00:02:21,940 --> 00:02:25,520
That's what's kind of been so disconcerting for me

61
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:26,660
as we've studied these parables

62
00:02:26,660 --> 00:02:28,920
is they really do not give us the option

63
00:02:28,920 --> 00:02:29,920
of sitting on the fence.

64
00:02:29,920 --> 00:02:31,740
You're either all in or you're all out.

65
00:02:31,740 --> 00:02:36,440
Which will you choose is at the root of the parables

66
00:02:36,440 --> 00:02:41,100
what Jesus wants us to be interacting with.

67
00:02:41,100 --> 00:02:42,340
And so my prayer is that this series

68
00:02:42,340 --> 00:02:44,380
has deepened our understanding of God's kingdom

69
00:02:44,380 --> 00:02:48,560
and motivated us to view ourselves

70
00:02:48,560 --> 00:02:50,240
as an answer to our own prayers.

71
00:02:50,240 --> 00:02:51,980
When we pray, your kingdom come,

72
00:02:51,980 --> 00:02:54,560
your will be done on earth as it is in heaven.

73
00:02:54,560 --> 00:02:58,160
May we view that ourselves as we live into the kingdom

74
00:02:58,160 --> 00:02:59,440
and answer to that prayer,

75
00:02:59,440 --> 00:03:01,620
that we are participating with God

76
00:03:01,620 --> 00:03:05,240
as he brings his kingdom on earth as it is in heaven.

77
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:06,300
So that's been the goal.

78
00:03:06,300 --> 00:03:09,960
Hopefully that's landed in some way, shape, or form for you.

79
00:03:10,340 --> 00:03:13,740
If not, send me an email and we'll talk about it.

80
00:03:13,740 --> 00:03:14,520
Sound good?

81
00:03:14,520 --> 00:03:16,440
All right, let's pray.

82
00:03:16,440 --> 00:03:18,520
And we'll move into our last parable.

83
00:03:18,520 --> 00:03:20,560
Father in heaven,

84
00:03:20,560 --> 00:03:26,740
we thank you for the surprising arrival of your kingdom.

85
00:03:26,740 --> 00:03:32,400
God, that you rode in on a donkey

86
00:03:32,400 --> 00:03:35,580
to chants of Hosanna.

87
00:03:35,580 --> 00:03:39,340
Everybody thinking the kingdom was coming in power

88
00:03:39,340 --> 00:03:43,440
and it came in sacrificial love.

89
00:03:43,440 --> 00:03:47,840
God, the kingdom came in such a surprising way

90
00:03:47,840 --> 00:03:51,940
that the Son of God laid down his life for us.

91
00:03:51,940 --> 00:03:55,240
And then the most unexpected plot twist

92
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:56,440
in all of human history

93
00:03:56,440 --> 00:03:58,720
was not contained by that grave.

94
00:04:00,260 --> 00:04:01,760
God, you rose from the dead.

95
00:04:01,760 --> 00:04:06,700
Solidifying the reality of your kingdom

96
00:04:06,700 --> 00:04:08,060
from now until you return.

97
00:04:08,060 --> 00:04:12,520
God, in the ethic of your kingdom

98
00:04:12,520 --> 00:04:14,360
is the same way that you established it.

99
00:04:14,360 --> 00:04:15,680
It is sacrificial love.

100
00:04:15,680 --> 00:04:17,500
It is laying down our life for our neighbors.

101
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:21,020
And that is a hard call.

102
00:04:22,880 --> 00:04:25,940
But nothing on earth is worthy

103
00:04:25,940 --> 00:04:28,600
of our time, attention, and resources

104
00:04:28,600 --> 00:04:29,940
than that reality.

105
00:04:29,940 --> 00:04:31,640
And so remind us of that this morning.

106
00:04:31,640 --> 00:04:34,220
And God, for those of us who are wrestling

107
00:04:34,220 --> 00:04:36,760
with the invitation to your kingdom,

108
00:04:36,760 --> 00:04:39,280
for those of us that might find ourselves

109
00:04:39,280 --> 00:04:40,920
on that fence with one foot in

110
00:04:40,920 --> 00:04:41,880
and with one foot out,

111
00:04:41,880 --> 00:04:45,140
or for those of us that have decided we're out,

112
00:04:45,140 --> 00:04:46,280
we're not interested,

113
00:04:46,280 --> 00:04:49,440
God, may this morning be an opportunity

114
00:04:49,440 --> 00:04:51,800
for us to be re-invited

115
00:04:51,800 --> 00:04:53,520
to embrace your kingdom fully.

116
00:04:53,520 --> 00:04:57,800
Your glory for our neighbor's good.

117
00:04:57,800 --> 00:05:00,520
In Jesus' name I pray, amen.

118
00:05:00,520 --> 00:05:04,780
If you wanna follow along,

119
00:05:04,780 --> 00:05:07,480
Matthew chapter 25 is where we're gonna get to.

120
00:05:07,480 --> 00:05:09,560
Matthew chapter 25, starting in verse 14.

121
00:05:09,560 --> 00:05:10,660
I don't know how many of you,

122
00:05:10,660 --> 00:05:13,720
how good your memories are.

123
00:05:13,720 --> 00:05:15,340
Raise your hand if you got a really good memory.

124
00:05:17,340 --> 00:05:20,340
That's impressive, I'm so jealous of all of you

125
00:05:20,340 --> 00:05:22,080
because I have a terrible memory,

126
00:05:22,080 --> 00:05:24,200
especially when it comes to my childhood.

127
00:05:24,200 --> 00:05:25,500
Like I try and think back

128
00:05:25,500 --> 00:05:27,860
to some memories of my childhood

129
00:05:27,860 --> 00:05:29,320
and I just don't have a lot

130
00:05:29,320 --> 00:05:30,840
of vivid concrete memories.

131
00:05:30,840 --> 00:05:32,660
I have lots of highlight clips, right?

132
00:05:32,660 --> 00:05:34,860
Like I can roll some highlight clips

133
00:05:34,860 --> 00:05:36,860
of my childhood playing around

134
00:05:36,860 --> 00:05:38,220
in the backyard and all of those things.

135
00:05:38,220 --> 00:05:39,880
But when it comes to concrete moments,

136
00:05:39,880 --> 00:05:42,580
outside of the incredible things

137
00:05:42,580 --> 00:05:43,980
that I did in peewee sports,

138
00:05:43,980 --> 00:05:46,800
I have vivid memories of those.

139
00:05:46,880 --> 00:05:50,000
But other than that, that was a joke, kind of.

140
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:52,280
We have a lot of home videos,

141
00:05:52,280 --> 00:05:54,960
so it's less memories and more I've rewatched myself.

142
00:05:54,960 --> 00:05:57,840
But anyway, that was not in the notes.

143
00:05:57,840 --> 00:06:02,200
Okay, a few of my most concrete memories

144
00:06:02,200 --> 00:06:04,220
are the first day that I went to public school.

145
00:06:04,220 --> 00:06:06,160
I was homeschooled, kindergarten and first grade

146
00:06:06,160 --> 00:06:07,100
and some of you are thinking,

147
00:06:07,100 --> 00:06:08,100
okay, that makes sense.

148
00:06:10,780 --> 00:06:13,500
I cannot spell and my mom makes fun of me for that

149
00:06:13,500 --> 00:06:15,480
and then I remind her that she taught me to spell.

150
00:06:15,480 --> 00:06:17,620
So there's that.

151
00:06:17,620 --> 00:06:20,760
But I remember like the first time getting on a school bus,

152
00:06:20,760 --> 00:06:23,340
the first time ushered into this big cafeteria

153
00:06:23,340 --> 00:06:25,380
where everybody knew everybody except for me,

154
00:06:25,380 --> 00:06:27,500
that was a really vivid memory.

155
00:06:27,500 --> 00:06:33,120
Another one, the first drive I got to take in my car

156
00:06:33,120 --> 00:06:34,880
on my own with nobody else.

157
00:06:34,880 --> 00:06:40,500
I had this vivid memory of backing up my 1996 GeoTracker

158
00:06:40,500 --> 00:06:43,280
and taking off to nowhere.

159
00:06:43,280 --> 00:06:44,720
I wasn't even going anywhere.

160
00:06:44,720 --> 00:06:49,620
I just wanted to go somewhere in the 96 GeoTracker.

161
00:06:49,620 --> 00:06:51,440
Yes, I wish I still had that thing.

162
00:06:51,440 --> 00:06:52,380
That thing was beautiful.

163
00:06:52,380 --> 00:06:54,400
Four cylinders almost got up the hill.

164
00:06:55,680 --> 00:06:58,460
I mean, we're 6,000 RPMs at 45 miles an hour

165
00:06:58,460 --> 00:06:59,840
headed to church in Back Creek.

166
00:06:59,840 --> 00:07:01,000
It was awesome.

167
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:05,540
And then one of the other ones is being left alone

168
00:07:05,540 --> 00:07:06,980
at home for the very first time.

169
00:07:06,980 --> 00:07:09,420
And I had an older brother,

170
00:07:09,420 --> 00:07:11,600
so I always thought I was ready for things

171
00:07:11,600 --> 00:07:12,940
before I actually was, right?

172
00:07:12,940 --> 00:07:15,260
I watched him do all of these awesome things

173
00:07:15,260 --> 00:07:17,460
and I'm like, I should be, I'm staying at home by myself.

174
00:07:17,460 --> 00:07:18,880
My mom's like, no, you're not.

175
00:07:18,880 --> 00:07:20,340
You're not.

176
00:07:20,340 --> 00:07:23,120
But finally, I remember the time when it arrived,

177
00:07:23,120 --> 00:07:26,420
when it was my opportunity to get to stay at home.

178
00:07:26,420 --> 00:07:28,360
There was a tremendous amount of excitement

179
00:07:28,360 --> 00:07:30,000
along with a little bit of unease

180
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:32,040
because I knew, like Donovan said,

181
00:07:32,040 --> 00:07:33,360
it comes, or like Michelle said,

182
00:07:33,360 --> 00:07:35,260
it comes with some responsibility.

183
00:07:35,260 --> 00:07:38,040
It comes with some accountability, right?

184
00:07:38,040 --> 00:07:40,600
If mom and dad come home and the house is in flames,

185
00:07:40,600 --> 00:07:41,920
it's on me.

186
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:44,960
So as much as I longed for this freedom,

187
00:07:44,960 --> 00:07:47,100
I also knew that it came with some responsibility

188
00:07:47,100 --> 00:07:48,000
and some accountability.

189
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:50,260
And as we approach our parable this morning,

190
00:07:51,580 --> 00:07:55,520
this is the backdrop that Jesus has for this parable,

191
00:07:55,520 --> 00:07:57,340
that he's speaking to his disciples

192
00:07:57,340 --> 00:07:59,080
as he is about to leave.

193
00:07:59,080 --> 00:08:00,660
He is warning them that he is going,

194
00:08:00,660 --> 00:08:03,620
that he is going to leave them here on purpose,

195
00:08:03,620 --> 00:08:04,440
on a mission.

196
00:08:04,440 --> 00:08:07,580
And this is a gift to them.

197
00:08:07,580 --> 00:08:09,940
It is a gift to the world around them.

198
00:08:09,940 --> 00:08:13,660
And it is a gift that comes with tremendous responsibility

199
00:08:13,660 --> 00:08:15,180
and accountability.

200
00:08:15,180 --> 00:08:17,780
And so as we approach this parable this morning,

201
00:08:17,780 --> 00:08:21,180
I want us to think about that backdrop in our heads.

202
00:08:21,180 --> 00:08:23,620
And let's go ahead and read Matthew chapter 25,

203
00:08:23,620 --> 00:08:25,580
starting in verse 14.

204
00:08:25,580 --> 00:08:27,180
Jesus tells this story.

205
00:08:27,180 --> 00:08:27,820
He says, again,

206
00:08:27,820 --> 00:08:30,580
the kingdom will be like a man going on a journey

207
00:08:30,580 --> 00:08:35,220
who called his servants and entrusted his wealth to them.

208
00:08:35,220 --> 00:08:37,360
He entrusted his wealth to them.

209
00:08:37,360 --> 00:08:40,320
To one, he gave five bags of gold,

210
00:08:40,320 --> 00:08:41,460
to another two,

211
00:08:41,460 --> 00:08:43,580
and to another one bag each,

212
00:08:43,580 --> 00:08:45,300
according to his ability.

213
00:08:46,100 --> 00:08:47,460
Then he went on his journey.

214
00:08:47,460 --> 00:08:50,180
The man who had received five bags of gold

215
00:08:50,180 --> 00:08:53,060
went at once and put his money to work

216
00:08:53,060 --> 00:08:54,540
and gained five bags more.

217
00:08:54,540 --> 00:08:57,700
So also the one with two bags of gold money

218
00:08:57,700 --> 00:09:00,320
went to work and gained two more.

219
00:09:00,320 --> 00:09:03,340
But the man who had received one bag went off

220
00:09:03,340 --> 00:09:05,140
and dug a hole in the ground,

221
00:09:05,140 --> 00:09:07,020
and he hid his master's money.

222
00:09:07,020 --> 00:09:10,620
After a long time,

223
00:09:10,620 --> 00:09:13,080
the master of those servants returned

224
00:09:13,080 --> 00:09:14,600
and settled accounts with them.

225
00:09:14,660 --> 00:09:16,760
The man who had received five bags of gold

226
00:09:16,760 --> 00:09:18,660
brought five more,

227
00:09:18,660 --> 00:09:19,040
and he said,

228
00:09:19,040 --> 00:09:21,540
Master, you have entrusted me with five bags of gold.

229
00:09:21,540 --> 00:09:23,320
See, I have brought you five more.

230
00:09:23,320 --> 00:09:24,160
His master replied,

231
00:09:24,160 --> 00:09:26,480
Well done, good and faithful servant.

232
00:09:26,480 --> 00:09:28,980
You have been faithful with a few things.

233
00:09:28,980 --> 00:09:32,120
Also, this master and I need to meet

234
00:09:32,120 --> 00:09:33,660
because five bags of gold

235
00:09:33,660 --> 00:09:35,460
is not a few things in my economy,

236
00:09:35,460 --> 00:09:36,040
but okay.

237
00:09:36,040 --> 00:09:38,020
You've been faithful with a few things.

238
00:09:38,060 --> 00:09:39,560
I will put you in charge of many things.

239
00:09:39,560 --> 00:09:41,600
Come, share in your master's joy,

240
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:42,560
your master's happiness.

241
00:09:42,560 --> 00:09:45,720
The man with two bags of gold also came.

242
00:09:45,720 --> 00:09:47,180
Master, he said,

243
00:09:47,180 --> 00:09:48,840
You entrusted me with two bags of gold.

244
00:09:48,840 --> 00:09:50,560
See, I have gained two more.

245
00:09:50,560 --> 00:09:51,420
His master replied,

246
00:09:51,420 --> 00:09:53,580
Well done, good and faithful servant.

247
00:09:53,580 --> 00:09:55,180
You have been faithful with a few things.

248
00:09:55,180 --> 00:09:57,680
I will put you in charge of many things.

249
00:09:57,680 --> 00:10:00,200
Come and share in your master's happiness.

250
00:10:00,200 --> 00:10:02,980
Then, again, parables are hard, remember?

251
00:10:02,980 --> 00:10:06,200
The man who had received one bag of gold came

252
00:10:06,200 --> 00:10:06,580
and he said,

253
00:10:06,580 --> 00:10:09,000
Master, I knew that you were a hard man,

254
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:11,180
harvesting where you have not sown

255
00:10:11,180 --> 00:10:13,200
and gathering where you have not scattered seeds.

256
00:10:13,200 --> 00:10:14,760
So I was afraid

257
00:10:14,760 --> 00:10:17,740
and I went out and hid your gold in the ground.

258
00:10:17,740 --> 00:10:19,520
See, here is what belongs to you.

259
00:10:19,520 --> 00:10:21,440
His master replied,

260
00:10:21,440 --> 00:10:23,360
You wicked and lazy servant.

261
00:10:23,360 --> 00:10:26,780
So you knew that I harvested where I did not sow

262
00:10:26,780 --> 00:10:28,500
and gather where I did not scatter seed.

263
00:10:28,500 --> 00:10:30,900
Well then, you should have put my money

264
00:10:30,900 --> 00:10:32,360
on deposit with the bankers

265
00:10:32,360 --> 00:10:33,820
so that when I returned,

266
00:10:33,820 --> 00:10:36,280
I would have received with it interest.

267
00:10:36,280 --> 00:10:38,940
So take the bag of gold from him

268
00:10:38,940 --> 00:10:40,760
and give it to the one who has 10 bags

269
00:10:40,760 --> 00:10:42,600
for whoever has will be given more

270
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:44,120
and they will have an abundance

271
00:10:44,120 --> 00:10:45,460
and whoever does not have,

272
00:10:45,460 --> 00:10:48,220
even what they have will be taken from them

273
00:10:48,220 --> 00:10:51,120
and throw that worthless servant

274
00:10:51,120 --> 00:10:52,700
outside into the darkness

275
00:10:52,700 --> 00:10:56,560
where there will be weeping and gnashing of teeth.

276
00:10:56,560 --> 00:10:58,380
This is the word of the Lord.

277
00:10:58,500 --> 00:11:01,020
Thanks be to God.

278
00:11:01,020 --> 00:11:05,400
Yeah, it's a tough one

279
00:11:05,400 --> 00:11:09,140
but I think if we give it the time it needs,

280
00:11:09,140 --> 00:11:10,720
we should be able to walk out of here

281
00:11:10,720 --> 00:11:12,180
more encouraged than discouraged.

282
00:11:12,180 --> 00:11:13,500
Sound good?

283
00:11:13,500 --> 00:11:14,540
Cool.

284
00:11:14,540 --> 00:11:18,040
Last week, we covered one of Christ's final parables.

285
00:11:18,040 --> 00:11:20,660
We're still in the final week of Christ's life

286
00:11:20,660 --> 00:11:23,480
and he told three intentional parables

287
00:11:23,480 --> 00:11:24,320
back to back to back

288
00:11:24,320 --> 00:11:27,060
directly aimed at the corrupt Jewish leadership

289
00:11:27,060 --> 00:11:29,880
which follows, that's Matthew 22,

290
00:11:29,880 --> 00:11:32,120
which follows by Matthew chapter 24

291
00:11:32,120 --> 00:11:33,580
which if I can be honest,

292
00:11:33,580 --> 00:11:36,320
Matthew chapter 24 is one of the most difficult chapters

293
00:11:36,320 --> 00:11:38,140
to understand in all of the New Testament.

294
00:11:38,140 --> 00:11:40,280
So if you're bored this week,

295
00:11:40,280 --> 00:11:41,780
have fun.

296
00:11:41,780 --> 00:11:43,600
Send me some email.

297
00:11:43,700 --> 00:11:44,220
No, don't.

298
00:11:44,220 --> 00:11:45,460
Don't send me some email.

299
00:11:45,460 --> 00:11:47,460
But I'll be honest with you,

300
00:11:47,460 --> 00:11:49,860
I spent more time trying to understand Matthew 24

301
00:11:49,860 --> 00:11:52,120
so that I could understand the context of this parable

302
00:11:52,120 --> 00:11:53,180
than I did the parable itself.

303
00:11:53,180 --> 00:11:54,560
Matthew 24 is extremely difficult.

304
00:11:54,560 --> 00:11:58,160
But I think what I settled on

305
00:11:58,160 --> 00:12:01,300
is ultimately what Jesus is doing

306
00:12:01,300 --> 00:12:03,000
is after he tells these three parables

307
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:05,060
aimed at the Jewish leadership

308
00:12:05,060 --> 00:12:06,200
and their corrupt nature

309
00:12:06,200 --> 00:12:06,760
and he's saying,

310
00:12:06,980 --> 00:12:08,740
this is your last chance to repent.

311
00:12:08,740 --> 00:12:11,760
This is your last opportunity to come back.

312
00:12:11,760 --> 00:12:13,320
And if you don't,

313
00:12:13,320 --> 00:12:16,320
I'm going to take away your leadership.

314
00:12:16,320 --> 00:12:17,860
I'm gonna take away your responsibility.

315
00:12:17,860 --> 00:12:19,760
And so after this, chapter 24,

316
00:12:19,760 --> 00:12:22,020
Jesus gives a shocking prediction.

317
00:12:22,020 --> 00:12:26,480
He very clearly and prophetically prophesies

318
00:12:26,480 --> 00:12:28,880
that the temple is going to be destroyed

319
00:12:28,880 --> 00:12:31,080
before the disciples die.

320
00:12:31,080 --> 00:12:32,260
He says,

321
00:12:32,260 --> 00:12:33,400
this temple,

322
00:12:33,400 --> 00:12:34,260
these stones,

323
00:12:34,260 --> 00:12:35,160
they're gonna be ripped down.

324
00:12:35,160 --> 00:12:38,280
These leaders who I just told these three parables against,

325
00:12:38,280 --> 00:12:40,800
their leadership is going to be taken away

326
00:12:40,800 --> 00:12:43,840
because they have not submitted to my kingdom.

327
00:12:43,840 --> 00:12:47,940
And in shocking Jesus fashion,

328
00:12:47,940 --> 00:12:49,520
you might be surprised to know,

329
00:12:49,520 --> 00:12:51,440
it happened, right?

330
00:12:51,440 --> 00:12:54,300
Rome comes in in 70 AD and destroys the temple

331
00:12:54,300 --> 00:12:57,220
and the leadership no longer have any sway

332
00:12:57,220 --> 00:12:58,440
over the nation of Israel.

333
00:12:58,440 --> 00:12:59,900
It's all taken away from them.

334
00:12:59,900 --> 00:13:02,300
This is a prediction that Jesus makes.

335
00:13:02,300 --> 00:13:04,360
And so when he makes this prediction,

336
00:13:04,480 --> 00:13:05,820
his disciples pull him aside,

337
00:13:05,820 --> 00:13:08,400
slightly uncomfortable with chapter 24,

338
00:13:08,400 --> 00:13:11,260
probably more uncomfortable with chapter 24 than I am.

339
00:13:11,260 --> 00:13:12,900
And they ask him some questions.

340
00:13:12,900 --> 00:13:13,840
What's going on here?

341
00:13:13,840 --> 00:13:14,460
What do you mean?

342
00:13:14,460 --> 00:13:16,760
They ask him,

343
00:13:16,760 --> 00:13:19,500
when is this going to happen?

344
00:13:19,500 --> 00:13:21,180
And how does this have to interact

345
00:13:21,180 --> 00:13:22,980
with your coming again,

346
00:13:22,980 --> 00:13:24,140
your second coming?

347
00:13:24,140 --> 00:13:25,000
They use the language,

348
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:26,840
the end of the age.

349
00:13:26,840 --> 00:13:29,160
The disciples likely thought

350
00:13:29,160 --> 00:13:30,480
that if the temple was destroyed,

351
00:13:30,480 --> 00:13:32,740
this would be the straw that broke the camel's back

352
00:13:32,740 --> 00:13:34,720
and it would trigger the end of the age.

353
00:13:34,720 --> 00:13:36,800
See, for 1,500 years,

354
00:13:36,800 --> 00:13:39,040
all of worship of Yahweh was rooted

355
00:13:39,040 --> 00:13:40,460
in the tabernacle and the temple.

356
00:13:40,460 --> 00:13:42,900
With no temple and no priest,

357
00:13:42,900 --> 00:13:44,080
worship would be impossible

358
00:13:44,080 --> 00:13:46,560
and it almost would certainly usher

359
00:13:46,560 --> 00:13:49,880
in God's rule and reign for all eternity.

360
00:13:49,880 --> 00:13:51,820
And this is where it gets interesting

361
00:13:51,820 --> 00:13:53,340
because Jesus responds by saying,

362
00:13:53,520 --> 00:13:55,040
yes, the temple will be destroyed

363
00:13:55,040 --> 00:13:56,340
in this generation,

364
00:13:56,340 --> 00:13:58,280
but the second coming

365
00:13:58,280 --> 00:13:59,840
and the destruction of the temple

366
00:13:59,840 --> 00:14:00,800
are not connected.

367
00:14:00,800 --> 00:14:02,600
As a matter of fact,

368
00:14:02,600 --> 00:14:04,020
he very intentionally says

369
00:14:04,020 --> 00:14:05,820
there's gonna be a long period of time

370
00:14:05,820 --> 00:14:07,300
in between the destruction of the temple

371
00:14:07,300 --> 00:14:08,160
and my second coming.

372
00:14:08,160 --> 00:14:09,820
And he makes it very clear

373
00:14:09,820 --> 00:14:11,320
that nobody knows

374
00:14:11,320 --> 00:14:14,060
when the second coming is happening.

375
00:14:14,060 --> 00:14:16,840
So if you spend time,

376
00:14:16,840 --> 00:14:18,340
this is free, okay?

377
00:14:18,340 --> 00:14:21,060
If you spend a lot of time on YouTube,

378
00:14:21,400 --> 00:14:22,660
listening to people telling you

379
00:14:22,660 --> 00:14:24,640
all about how Jesus is gonna come back soon

380
00:14:24,640 --> 00:14:25,800
because of things that are happening

381
00:14:25,800 --> 00:14:27,140
around the world,

382
00:14:27,140 --> 00:14:30,120
Jesus says, don't worry about it.

383
00:14:30,120 --> 00:14:33,400
You're wasting your time, okay?

384
00:14:33,400 --> 00:14:35,760
He will return

385
00:14:35,760 --> 00:14:37,840
and he might return tomorrow

386
00:14:37,840 --> 00:14:39,820
and we should be anticipatory about that.

387
00:14:39,820 --> 00:14:41,480
I'm not saying don't think about Christ coming,

388
00:14:41,480 --> 00:14:42,680
think about Christ coming,

389
00:14:42,680 --> 00:14:43,900
but don't try and figure out

390
00:14:43,900 --> 00:14:44,520
when it's gonna happen

391
00:14:44,520 --> 00:14:45,820
because he says nobody knows

392
00:14:45,820 --> 00:14:46,760
when it's gonna happen.

393
00:14:46,760 --> 00:14:48,720
So if your friend with 10,000 subscribers

394
00:14:48,720 --> 00:14:49,760
on YouTube tells you

395
00:14:49,760 --> 00:14:50,800
he knows when it's gonna happen,

396
00:14:52,400 --> 00:14:54,420
listen, Jesus, red letters, okay?

397
00:14:54,420 --> 00:14:56,180
No one's free.

398
00:14:56,180 --> 00:14:59,200
And what he says is he says,

399
00:14:59,200 --> 00:15:00,600
now when the temple is destroyed,

400
00:15:00,600 --> 00:15:02,380
when the priest leadership is taken away,

401
00:15:02,380 --> 00:15:04,700
the responsibility for true worship of Yahweh

402
00:15:04,700 --> 00:15:06,320
will fall to you, the disciples,

403
00:15:06,320 --> 00:15:08,280
and all who have embraced God's kingdom.

404
00:15:08,280 --> 00:15:09,580
You will be priests.

405
00:15:09,580 --> 00:15:10,800
We will be priests.

406
00:15:10,800 --> 00:15:12,700
All of us who have embraced God's kingdom

407
00:15:12,700 --> 00:15:13,380
will be priests.

408
00:15:13,380 --> 00:15:15,560
We will carry forward the mission of God

409
00:15:15,560 --> 00:15:16,640
and the worship of Yahweh

410
00:15:16,640 --> 00:15:18,800
from Jerusalem to Judea,

411
00:15:18,800 --> 00:15:20,400
to the ends of the earth.

412
00:15:20,700 --> 00:15:22,720
This is what he's setting up with these parables.

413
00:15:22,720 --> 00:15:24,220
He tells three parables

414
00:15:24,220 --> 00:15:26,460
and they are directly aimed at his disciples,

415
00:15:26,460 --> 00:15:28,540
directly preparing for them

416
00:15:28,540 --> 00:15:29,800
for this period of time

417
00:15:29,800 --> 00:15:31,300
after the destruction of the temple

418
00:15:31,300 --> 00:15:33,660
and until his second coming returns.

419
00:15:33,660 --> 00:15:35,200
So we've talked a lot

420
00:15:35,200 --> 00:15:36,340
as we've read the parables.

421
00:15:36,340 --> 00:15:37,760
We've said we need to understand them

422
00:15:37,760 --> 00:15:38,940
in their original context

423
00:15:38,940 --> 00:15:40,840
before we can understand them for ourselves.

424
00:15:40,840 --> 00:15:43,440
And pretty much every parable

425
00:15:43,440 --> 00:15:44,340
we've covered so far

426
00:15:44,340 --> 00:15:45,980
was directed at a group of people

427
00:15:45,980 --> 00:15:47,240
that are not us.

428
00:15:47,240 --> 00:15:50,140
But I would argue that these parables,

429
00:15:50,140 --> 00:15:52,100
more than any other parables,

430
00:15:52,100 --> 00:15:54,300
are directed at a group of people

431
00:15:54,300 --> 00:15:56,000
that are very similar to us.

432
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:58,460
He is directing these parables

433
00:15:58,460 --> 00:16:00,320
to faithful followers of Jesus,

434
00:16:00,320 --> 00:16:02,420
faithful followers of the kingdom

435
00:16:02,420 --> 00:16:04,200
who are awaiting Christ's second return.

436
00:16:05,240 --> 00:16:08,620
And so we can almost interpret these parables

437
00:16:08,620 --> 00:16:11,200
as if they were written to us.

438
00:16:11,200 --> 00:16:14,980
What will we do with what God has given us

439
00:16:14,980 --> 00:16:17,180
as we await his return?

440
00:16:17,180 --> 00:16:20,780
This is the overarching point of the parable.

441
00:16:20,880 --> 00:16:23,240
And just like me being left at home

442
00:16:23,240 --> 00:16:24,080
for the first time,

443
00:16:24,080 --> 00:16:25,080
to me was a gift

444
00:16:25,080 --> 00:16:27,600
of newfound freedom and responsibility.

445
00:16:27,600 --> 00:16:29,800
It was a gift that came with responsibility

446
00:16:29,800 --> 00:16:31,120
and accountability.

447
00:16:31,120 --> 00:16:33,500
So too, Jesus says in this parable,

448
00:16:33,500 --> 00:16:36,760
is me ascending into heaven,

449
00:16:36,760 --> 00:16:38,580
sending the Holy Spirit to you

450
00:16:38,580 --> 00:16:40,760
and entrusting you with the kingdom of God

451
00:16:40,760 --> 00:16:41,560
until I return.

452
00:16:41,560 --> 00:16:43,140
It is a gift

453
00:16:43,140 --> 00:16:45,220
that comes with responsibility

454
00:16:45,220 --> 00:16:46,480
and accountability.

455
00:16:46,480 --> 00:16:49,640
And that is the overarching narrative

456
00:16:49,640 --> 00:16:50,440
of this parable.

457
00:16:50,520 --> 00:16:52,340
So let's unpack it one point at a time.

458
00:16:52,340 --> 00:16:53,200
First, the gift.

459
00:16:53,200 --> 00:16:57,920
A master gives his servants

460
00:16:57,920 --> 00:17:00,180
an incredible amount of money.

461
00:17:00,180 --> 00:17:02,280
Scholars debate exactly

462
00:17:02,280 --> 00:17:04,640
over how much money each talent was.

463
00:17:04,640 --> 00:17:05,720
Talent is just a number,

464
00:17:05,720 --> 00:17:07,360
a metric of measurement.

465
00:17:07,360 --> 00:17:09,380
Is that the right way to say that?

466
00:17:09,380 --> 00:17:10,200
Metric of measurement?

467
00:17:10,200 --> 00:17:11,560
Yeah?

468
00:17:11,560 --> 00:17:12,640
Okay, cool.

469
00:17:12,640 --> 00:17:14,040
We're gonna stick with it

470
00:17:14,040 --> 00:17:15,300
because I don't know another way to say it.

471
00:17:15,300 --> 00:17:19,280
And so some argue

472
00:17:19,280 --> 00:17:23,900
one talent is somewhere between five and 20 years wages

473
00:17:23,900 --> 00:17:25,340
for a normal worker.

474
00:17:25,340 --> 00:17:26,740
So let's just say 1 million,

475
00:17:26,740 --> 00:17:27,180
2 million,

476
00:17:27,180 --> 00:17:28,440
5 million dollars, right?

477
00:17:28,440 --> 00:17:30,000
It's a lot of money.

478
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:31,520
No matter whether you got the 1 million

479
00:17:31,520 --> 00:17:32,360
or the 5 million,

480
00:17:32,360 --> 00:17:33,320
you have been entrusted

481
00:17:33,320 --> 00:17:34,740
with a massive gift,

482
00:17:34,740 --> 00:17:36,380
a gift that servants of this time,

483
00:17:36,380 --> 00:17:37,760
they would have been trusted

484
00:17:37,760 --> 00:17:38,380
with these things.

485
00:17:38,380 --> 00:17:39,000
And the master says,

486
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:40,060
I'm entrusting you

487
00:17:40,060 --> 00:17:41,120
with this amount of wealth.

488
00:17:41,120 --> 00:17:42,240
You get to steward it.

489
00:17:42,320 --> 00:17:43,360
You get to use it.

490
00:17:43,360 --> 00:17:45,820
Think of it as yours.

491
00:17:45,820 --> 00:17:48,380
It is a gift.

492
00:17:48,380 --> 00:17:50,180
Now,

493
00:17:50,180 --> 00:17:51,920
the disciples hearing this parable

494
00:17:51,920 --> 00:17:54,480
would have been way less pumped

495
00:17:54,480 --> 00:17:55,940
about Jesus leaving them

496
00:17:55,940 --> 00:17:57,220
than I was about my parents

497
00:17:57,220 --> 00:17:58,220
leaving me at home alone.

498
00:17:58,220 --> 00:17:59,140
Right?

499
00:17:59,140 --> 00:18:00,540
The disciples are like,

500
00:18:00,540 --> 00:18:00,740
Jesus,

501
00:18:00,940 --> 00:18:01,540
no,

502
00:18:01,540 --> 00:18:02,500
don't leave.

503
00:18:02,500 --> 00:18:04,180
Why are you going?

504
00:18:04,180 --> 00:18:05,080
You don't need to go.

505
00:18:05,080 --> 00:18:05,540
You're here.

506
00:18:05,540 --> 00:18:06,820
The Son of God is here.

507
00:18:06,820 --> 00:18:07,840
The kingdom has come.

508
00:18:07,840 --> 00:18:09,000
This is fine.

509
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:10,760
Let's do it this way.

510
00:18:10,760 --> 00:18:12,300
But later in the Gospel of John,

511
00:18:12,300 --> 00:18:13,600
Jesus tells his disciples

512
00:18:13,600 --> 00:18:14,260
very clearly,

513
00:18:14,260 --> 00:18:15,060
it is better

514
00:18:15,060 --> 00:18:16,220
that I go

515
00:18:16,220 --> 00:18:17,900
so that the Holy Spirit

516
00:18:17,900 --> 00:18:18,900
can come.

517
00:18:18,900 --> 00:18:20,880
Jesus leaving

518
00:18:20,880 --> 00:18:22,220
after his resurrection

519
00:18:22,220 --> 00:18:23,420
and ascending into heaven

520
00:18:23,420 --> 00:18:24,440
is a gift

521
00:18:24,440 --> 00:18:26,040
and we have to see it that way.

522
00:18:26,040 --> 00:18:27,180
We have to view it that way

523
00:18:27,180 --> 00:18:27,800
because if not,

524
00:18:27,800 --> 00:18:28,620
we will miss out

525
00:18:28,620 --> 00:18:29,540
on the things

526
00:18:29,540 --> 00:18:30,740
that we've been entrusted with.

527
00:18:30,740 --> 00:18:33,340
Not only does he tell the disciples

528
00:18:33,340 --> 00:18:34,120
it's better that I go

529
00:18:34,120 --> 00:18:35,000
that the Spirit can come

530
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:36,780
but what is increasingly becoming

531
00:18:36,780 --> 00:18:37,920
two of my favorite chapters

532
00:18:37,920 --> 00:18:38,760
in all of the Bible,

533
00:18:38,760 --> 00:18:40,220
Revelation chapter four and five

534
00:18:40,220 --> 00:18:41,140
show that Jesus

535
00:18:41,140 --> 00:18:42,480
is actually actively

536
00:18:42,480 --> 00:18:43,860
doing something in heaven

537
00:18:43,860 --> 00:18:44,920
bringing about

538
00:18:44,920 --> 00:18:45,920
his final restoration.

539
00:18:45,920 --> 00:18:47,620
Jesus needed to ascend to heaven

540
00:18:47,620 --> 00:18:48,720
to give us the Spirit

541
00:18:48,720 --> 00:18:50,380
to send us out on mission

542
00:18:50,380 --> 00:18:52,200
so that he could move forward

543
00:18:52,200 --> 00:18:53,640
the redemption plan of God.

544
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:55,260
Read Revelation four and five

545
00:18:55,260 --> 00:18:55,660
this week,

546
00:18:55,660 --> 00:18:56,780
not Matthew 24

547
00:18:56,780 --> 00:18:58,000
if you really want to be encouraged.

548
00:18:58,000 --> 00:18:58,520
I'm just kidding,

549
00:18:58,520 --> 00:18:59,100
do whatever you want

550
00:18:59,100 --> 00:19:01,220
but Revelation four and five,

551
00:19:01,220 --> 00:19:01,640
it's awesome.

552
00:19:01,640 --> 00:19:04,420
So he gives his servants

553
00:19:04,420 --> 00:19:05,900
a tremendous amount of money

554
00:19:05,900 --> 00:19:06,520
and I would argue

555
00:19:06,520 --> 00:19:07,360
the money represents

556
00:19:07,360 --> 00:19:08,700
really two different categories

557
00:19:08,700 --> 00:19:09,740
of giftings

